  "name": "Crumbling Castle",
  "type": "spell",
  "effects": [],
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p class=\"MsoNormal\">You conjure the image of a well articulated series of shapes into a structure that comes crumbling down upon your foes. Creatures in the target area must make a basic Reflex save or take 8d6 force damage. If your visionary skill is Crafting or Society, they take a -2 circumstance penalty to their save. </p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">You can add an ephemeral catalyst to enhance this spell. If you do, the target area becomes difficult terrain for the next minute.</p><hr><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>Heightened (+1)</strong> Increase the damage dealt by 2d6.</p>"
    },
